.TH DIPIDESCRAMBLE 1 "2026-08-17" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipidescramble \- standalone CAS validation client / descrambler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipidescramble
.B \-i
.I uri
.B \-k
.I keyfile
.B \-s
.I serial
.B \-e
.I emmfile
.B \-o
.I output
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipidescramble
is a standalone CAS validation client: it descrambles a
.BR dipitvhead / dipiradiohead -produced
(or any wire-compatible) DVB-CSA1/CSA2/CISSA/BISS transport stream, given
the device's RSA private key or a BISS session word. It is the
client-side counterpart to
.BR dipitvhead 's/ dipiradiohead 's
CAS muxer/scrambler, mainly meant for automated tests: reading a
(possibly) scrambled stream and writing it back out in the clear so the
result can be checked. The CAS scheme is auto-detected from the stream's
PMT
.B CA_descriptor
/
.BR scrambling_descriptor ;
.BR \-k / \-s / \-e
or the
.B \-\-biss*
options are only required once the stream turns out to need them.
.PP
For ECM/EMM-driven (SimulCrypt-style) CAS, decryption follows the
RSA -> BK -> SK -> CW key chain: EMM-U/EMM-G sections addressed to this
device (matched by
.BR \-s ,
its serial) are decrypted with the device's RSA private key
.RB ( \-k )
to recover the Bouquet Key (BK); the BK decrypts the ECM to recover the
Session Key/Word (SK); the SK in turn yields the Control Words (CW) used
to descramble the transport stream payload itself. An EMM cache
.RB ( \-e )
holds decrypted EMM-U/EMM-G state across restarts, so a test run does not
need to wait for the broadcast EMM carousel cadence (or
.BR \-u )
again. An optional unicast EMM pull
.RB ( \-u )
fetches EMMs once at startup instead of waiting on the carousel.
.PP
BISS (EBU Tech 3292) is supported directly without a device key: BISS1
Mode 1 (CSA1, 12 hex char Session Word,
.BR \-\-biss1\-sw ),
BISS2 Mode 1 or Mode E (CISSA, 32 hex char Session Word or Encrypted
Session Word + receiver ID,
.BR \-\-biss2\-sw / \-\-biss2\-esw / \-\-biss2\-id ),
and BISS2 Mode CA (RSA-OAEP receiver entitlement key,
.BR \-\-biss2\-ca\-key ),
which uses its own RSA-OAEP/AES-CBC/CISSA key hierarchy instead of the
generic ECM/EMM CAS path.
.PP
.B \-\-ecm\-profile
defines the internal formatting of an ECM payload (cipher, IV source,
padding, header fields, integrity check, and more) for CAS schemes whose
ECM layout is not hardcoded, since DVB-SimulCrypt leaves ECM payload
formatting undefined and
.BR dipitvhead / dipiradiohead
treat it as an opaque blob.
.PP
Known gaps shared with
.BR dipitvhead / dipiradiohead :
no ETSI TS 103 197 CSA3 or non-standard CSA2 modes, no BISS1 Mode E, no
BISS-CA group keys (device keys only), no eECMs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " " \fIuri\fR
Input:
.BR udp:// ,
.BR rtp:// ,
or
.B \-
for stdin. Required.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIpath\fR
Device RSA private key, PEM. Required for ECM/EMM-driven CAS.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-serial " " \fIid\fR
This device's serial, matched against EMM-U addressing. Required for
ECM/EMM-driven CAS.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-emm\-file " " \fIpath\fR
EMM cache: loaded on startup, rewritten on update. Required for
ECM/EMM-driven CAS.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-unicast\-emm " " \fIuri\fR
Unicast EMM pull endpoint, auth token as URI userinfo, e.g.
.IR https://<token>@<host>:<port>/device/<serial>/emm .
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Skip TLS verification for
.B \-u
/
.B \-\-unicast\-emm
and
.B \-o
.B rtmps://
(self-signed cert, hostname mismatch, expiry).
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-sw \fIhex32\fR
BISS2 Mode 1: 32 hex char Session Word.
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-esw \fIhex32\fR
BISS2 Mode E: 32 hex char Encrypted Session Word. Needs
.BR \-\-biss2\-id .
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-id \fIhex32\fR
BISS2 Mode E: 32 hex char receiver ID for
.BR \-\-biss2\-esw .
.TP
.B \-\-biss1\-sw \fIhex12\fR
Legacy BISS1 Mode 1: 12 hex char Session Word.
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-ca\-key \fIpath\fR
BISS Mode CA: receiver RSA private key, PEM.
.TP
.B \-\-ecm\-profile \fIspec\fR
ecm_profile template, comma-separated key=value (see
.B README.md
in the source tree).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fItarget\fR
Descrambled output, repeatable: a file path,
.B \-
for stdout, or
.BR rtmp(s):// .
An
.B rtmp(s)://
target is
.IR host [ : port ]/ app / key ,
carrying descrambled H.264/HEVC video plus AC-3/E-AC-3/AAC audio.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIfmt\fR
Output container:
.BR ts ", " mkv ", or " mka .
Default
.BR ts .
Raw
.B ts
and
.B rtmp(s)://
targets may mix;
.B mkv
/
.B mka
needs exactly one plain file target.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pmt\-pid " " \fIpid\fR|\fBall\fR
MPTS source only: pin one PMT pid, or descramble every program
.RB ( all ;
rejected with
.BR \-f\ mkv ).
Ignored (with a warning) on an SPTS source. If omitted on an MPTS source,
the tool fails early and lists the available programs.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-iface " " \fIiface\fR
Incoming multicast interface.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Periodic stats plus BK/SK/CW update lines on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fIwhen\fR
Colorize log output:
.BR auto ,
.BR always ,
or
.BR never .
Default
.BR auto .
.TP
.B \-\-max\-services \fIn\fR
Max services tracked in the EMM cache, 1..256. Default 32.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipidescramble \-i rtp://@239.0.0.1:1975 \-k device.key \-s e2e-01 \-e emm.cache \-o out.ts \-v
ECM/EMM-driven CAS: descramble using the device's private key, serial,
and an EMM cache, writing a plain
.B .ts
file.
.TP
.B dipidescramble \-i rtp://@239.0.0.1:1975 \-\-biss2\-sw 00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff \-o out.ts
BISS2 Mode 1: descramble with a known Session Word, no device key needed.
.TP
.B dipidescramble \-i rtp://@239.0.0.1:1975 \-\-biss2\-sw 00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff \-o rtmp://live.example.com/app/key
BISS2 Mode 1, pushing the descrambled stream live to an RTMP ingest
server instead of writing a file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
Non-zero on argument errors or decryption/I/O failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipitvhead (1),
.BR dipiradiohead (1),
.BR dipicam378 (1)
.PP
